      <div class="card step"><div class="year">1959</div><p>WHO resolution to eradicate smallpox globally.</p></div>
      <div class="card step"><div class="year">1967</div><p>WHO launches intensified eradication campaign.</p></div>
      <div class="card step"><div class="year">1977</div><p>Last natural case recorded in Somalia.</p></div>
      <div class="card step"><div class="year">1980</div><p>Global eradication certified worldwide.</p></div>
    </div>
    <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top:auto">
      <li>Eradication was feasible because smallpox infected only humans.</li>
      <li>Symptoms were distinctive, enabling rapid case detection.</li>
      <li>The vaccine was cheap, effective, and deployable at scale.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="content">
    <h2>Herd Immunity: How Vaccinating Many Protects the Most Vulnerable</h2>
