          <div class="dot vax">V</div><div class="dot vax">V</div><div class="dot vax">V</div><div class="dot vax">V</div><div class="dot vax">V</div><div class="dot vax">V</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top:0">
          <li>Vaccination reduces transmission chains across the population.</li>
          <li>Indirect protection shields people who cannot be vaccinated.</li>
          <li>Beneficiaries include newborns, immunocompromised people, and patients on chemotherapy.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="content">
    <h2>Gaps Persist: Pneumococcal Disease Shows Only 40% Case Reduction</h2>
    <div class="row" style="margin-top:clamp(8px,1vh,14px)">
      <div class="card" style="flex:1">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:clamp(18px,1.8vw,28px)">Incomplete disease control</h3>
        <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top:0">
          <li>Pneumococcal: 40.5% case reduction; 31.3% death reduction.</li>
          <li>Hepatitis A: 89% case reduction; 88.7% death reduction.</li>
          <li>Acute hepatitis B: 83.9% case reduction; 83.6% death reduction.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="flex:1">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:clamp(18px,1.8vw,28px)">Persistent barriers</h3>
        <ul class="bullets" style="margin-top:0">
          <li>Unequal global access to vaccines and delivery infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Supply shortages that leave children under-protected.</li>
          <li>Poor scientific understanding that reduces trust and uptake.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="content">
    <h2>Key Takeaways: Vaccines Have Eliminated Deadly Diseases — But the Job Isn’t Done</h2>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>US vaccination achieved 100% elimination of cases and deaths for diphtheria, smallpox, and acute polio.</li>
      <li>Development timelines collapsed from 105 years (typhoid) to under 1 year (COVID-19).</li>
      <li>State-level measles incidence dropped from 100–1,000+ per 100,000 pre-1963 to near zero after 1980 mandates.</li>
      <li>Herd immunity protects entire communities, especially those who cannot be vaccinated.</li>
      <li>Priority for health systems: improve access, coverage, and trust to close remaining gaps.</li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>
</body>
</html>
